WEBVTT

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.940
Have you ever wanted something so badly
you were willing to wait in a long line?

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.470
A ride at an amusement park?

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.700
To buy something special?

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.690
Or for ramen?

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.120
Finally, morning training's over.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.920
What should we do for lunch?

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.540
Any preference, Lee?

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:49.740
Let's see.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.610
Yesterday was pork curry.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.470
The day before was ground beef curry.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.810
And three days ago was green curry.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.640
I say today we go for it and 
get the ultimate curry!

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.580
It'll be great!

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.660
What is with all the curry this month?!

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.250
The curry festival needs to end!

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.440
Well, from a business point of view,

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.280
if we keep pushing curry, a food
company might sponsor the show—

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.760
Leave that to the producers.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.820
How about ramen?

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.540
Sold! Let's head to Ichiraku!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.250
For those who don't know,
Ichiraku is a famous restaurant...

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.130
...in the Hidden Leaf village,
and Naruto's first choice for ramen!

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:44.970
<b>Save Ichiraku Ramen!</b>

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.930
Ichiraku might go out of business?!

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:50.890
Unfortunately.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.260
A new ramen chain from the Flavor 
Village called Tasty Ramen...

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.390
...just opened a store directly 
across the street,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.880
and it's taking Ichiraku's customers.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.830
There's another ramen spot.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:06.040
But look at that line. 
This place must be way better!

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.620
People see that line 
and they hop right in.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.170
It's like lining up for that 
place is becoming a new trend.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:17.070
Anyway, because of them, 
no one's going to Ichiraku anymore.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.680
The old man's getting really depressed,

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.190
and I'm worried about him.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.210
People are suckers for famous 
names and long lines.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:29.210
It's always survival of the 
fittest in the business world.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.260
But this isn't fair.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.360
It's one thing if their 
food is better,

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.730
but for them to be winning on 
name recognition and trendiness?

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.690
Naruto!

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.400
You can count on us to 
help save Ichiraku!

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.660
Bushy-Brows... Let's do it!

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.160
I appreciate the offer.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.530
But making ramen is too hard for a...

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.760
...bunch of novices to waltz 
in and do it right away.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.130
Naruto, your skill lies 
in eating, not cooking!

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.130
Have no fear. We don't intend 
to change the flavor.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:05.990
Your ramen has been beloved 
by villagers for many years.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.430
Um, it looks like Naruto's the 
only one eating anything...

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.400
If you simply alter your 
business strategy a bit,

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.680
I guarantee you can beat Tasty Ramen!

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.360
Let's go for it, pops!

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:24.730
All right, I can't turn 
away such enthusiasm!

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.070
Let's give it our best shot!

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.750
The first step is to know thy enemy.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.200
Let's do some recon.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.900
I see, so we spy on their recipe—

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:37.710
Don't you dare!

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.850
First of all, the enemy 
will recognize us.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.220
And secondly, I don't think 
my stubborn old dad...

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.910
...is going to line up at a competitor's 
store and eat his food.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.510
He's already there?!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.340
Dad, have some pride!

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.690
You talk to him, Naru—

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.270
Not you, too!

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.640
Don't worry, Tenten.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:04.690
We don't need Naruto or Mr. Teuchi
to spy on the enemy's flavors.

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:05.310
Neji!

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.660
That's right.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.520
They don't know Neji's face,

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.680
he should be able to get a seat and—

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.620
Byakugan!

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.000
That's what you meant 
by spy on the flavor?!

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.630
Even if you can see the dish,

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.980
you still don't know what it tastes like!

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.750
It's a very thick, pork-based broth,

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.850
with two types of mackerel, 
bonito and vegetable dashi.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.890
Yet in spite of its heaviness, 
it has a smooth, mild flavor.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.130
You really can see the flavor?!

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.980
The Byakugan is so broken!

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:45.190
Okay, now we need to formulate a
"Double Fish Pork Ramen" counterattack.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.920
Huh? Since when are you so 
knowledgeable about ramen?

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:49.990
First!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.240
<b>Fried Rice</b>

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.240
<b>Sichuan 
Bean Curd 

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.240
<b>Veggies</b>

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.240
We need to come up with the right sides!

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.600
Indeed.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.690
Dumplings, gyoza, fried chicken...

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.170
There are a lot of good 
sides that go with ramen.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.870
It's true that we work very 
hard on our ramen dishes,

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:07.220
but tend to neglect the sides.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:07.880
And so!

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.590
<b>Barbecue Lunch Set</b>

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.590
I came up with a barbecue lunch set!

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:15.810
A lunch set is way beyond a side! 
That's a whole meal in itself!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.450
And to counter the enemy's thick broth...

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.560
No!

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.270
Dad!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.430
We need to lay the service on thick!

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:31.670
Your head is the only 
thick thing around here!

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:34.440
For some reason, I'm burning with youth!

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.250
Especially in the head area!

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.870
The wig is making you hot!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.120
Our enemy isn't just laying it on thick!

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.590
Don't forget they keep it in check 
with a smooth, mild flavor!

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:45.930
I remember.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:46.340
So...

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:49.150
Here!

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.010
A Can-Can girl?!

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:58.560
To balance our thicker service 
with something smoother.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.670
This isn't food service, it's fan service!

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.690
And this outfit shows no restraint!

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:04.690
Not here,

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:05.810
and not here!

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.720
There's nothing left to the imagination!

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:11.780
I guess I need to keep 
things in check more?

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:13.870
Here!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.530
A school swimsuit?!

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.960
Showing less skin doesn't fix 
the fundamental problem!

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:21.360
Even if we change the service,

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.180
it makes no difference 
if we have no customers.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.340
That's true.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.800
Why don't we use ringers?

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:31.150
Just seeing the line seems to 
draw people to the other place.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.890
That's true, there's some psychology to
making people want to stand in line.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.380
Ringers might be the ticket.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.730
I like it! Let's give it a try!

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:42.380
Here's our ringer!

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.350
We need more than her!

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.770
What the heck is going on here?

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.490
Er, sorry, Sakura...

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.850
No one's gonna line up 
just because of Sakura!

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:53.060
We did.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.100
She only works on you!

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.660
We're in, too!

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.240
Get back in the kitchen!

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:00.760
Who's gonna make the food?

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.380
Leave the cooking to me!

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.330
You leave it to the professionals!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:04.980
Professionals?

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:08.210
Now we just need to wait for 
the customers to roll in.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.280
Yeah!

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:13.720
But no customers came back to Ichiraku.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.610
Why didn't it work?

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.940
I think our business plan 
went down the wrong track.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:24.850
I'd say it went straight of the 
rails and flew off into space.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.690
I'm sorry, kids...

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.350
You tried so hard for me...

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:30.800
Pops...

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.440
I've got a lot of confidence in my dishes.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.160
I'm sad I'm not getting a 
chance to compete on flavor.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:42.120
They're all just lining up because 
of the name, or the line itself.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:43.880
If there was a way to make them realize...

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.570
...the food here is good without 
actually eating it...

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:47.460
Know it's good without eating...

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.480
We can! There's a way!

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:53.130
How so, Bushy-Brows?

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.590
Leave everything to me!

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:59.560
And so we're here to find the 
best ramen in the Leaf Village!

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.870
Our expert is the village's most well
respected gourmand, Choji Akimichi.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:07.520
Glad to be here.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.340
I'm gonna stuff myself silly!

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.510
What's the plan, Lee?

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.830
The only way to convince people 
of a restaurant's quality...

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.960
...is a positive review from 
a famous food critic.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.660
If such a critic were to sing its 
praises in front of that line...

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.000
Hey, that ramen place looks good!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.450
I'm going over there!

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:25.350
Me, too!

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:27.790
And bam.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:30.880
We'll have an even bigger line over here.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.100
But why Choji?

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.370
Choji is like the 
Guy Fieri of the village.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.510
Food always looks yummier when 
a fat person's enjoying it.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.290
I am not fat.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:43.930
I'm big-boned!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.890
Now let's all dig in!

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.740
Bon appétit!

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.620
This delicious!

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:53.080
What do you think, Mr. Nejiyama?

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.360
What? Me?!

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.200
Why Neji?

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.380
It's, um, I'd say...

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:03.530
It's Eight Trigrams and Sixty-Four 
Strikes of deliciousness!

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.630
That made no sense!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.510
It was the best I could do...

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:10.010
Being a food critic is so complex...

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.460
You're overthinking this!

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.470
What is all that?

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.920
I don't get it...

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.270
This is bad, Lee. 
They're getting turned off!

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:21.590
Another round, please!

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:23.130
<i>Nice, Choji!</i>

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:27.640
<i>If Choji eats a few bowls we can
convince people the ramen is that good!</i>

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.340
This barbecue lunch set 
is outta this world!

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.320
<i>He's not eating ramen!</i>

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.560
My brilliant side dish backfired...

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.720
You idiot, Lee, you stupid idiot!

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.340
We worked so hard and you ruined it!

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.640
I've got this!

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.100
Neji, please turn this around!

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.500
The flavor's Byakugan-tastic!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.140
That is the most confusing—

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:52.720
No, I'm trying to say the 
flavor is bright and clear—

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:55.290
No, there's nothing but a 
black void awaiting us...

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:00.300
Choji, please eat some ramen!

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.830
Wait, I'm not done—

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.380
Eat it and tell us what you think!

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.590
Let me finish my beef first!

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.020
The ramen!

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:13.680
Sakura, watch out!

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:14.980
I should've known!

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:19.240
Leaf Whirlwind!

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.650
Hey, this is really tasty!

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:29.490
I'm gonna check that 
place out. It's open!

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:30.710
Me, too!

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:36.890
Gimme ramen!

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.250
I want some ramen!

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.250
Dad!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.780
Naruto... Lee!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:45.680
Thank you!

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.780
Thus, Ichiraku escaped bankruptcy.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:55.060
<b>Sorry, Sold Out. 
-Ichiraku</b>

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:55.060
But the sudden upswing in customers...

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:59.170
...left Lee and the others 
with empty stomachs.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.990
I want my ramen!

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:13.450
Lee and his team are back from a mission.

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:16.810
Finally home...

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:19.500
That mission was brutal...

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.690
I need to get home and take a break.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:23.840
A break, huh?  Okay!

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.460
All right, I'll squeeze 
100 apples and make us...

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.200
...the most refreshing juice 
you've ever tasted!

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.310
That's no break. You're just painting
yourself into a corner again.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:36.770
I train my body even when I'm resting.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.900
Suddenly, I'm burning with passion!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.970
You don't have to burn up for this!

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:43.740
Can't you regulate your 
temperature better?

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:58.210
<b>Vacations are for Training!</b>

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.130
Bushy-Brows refuses to rest?

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.460
Yeah.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.620
Ever since fall began, 
it's been one event after another,

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:08.830
and he makes a big production 
out of all of them.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.600
Plus Guy Sensei always makes him...

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.790
...do these weird exercises 
with him on our days off.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:19.210
I'll say it's weird. What is this?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.730
I'm worried about his health.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:26.350
It's true. There is such
 a thing as over training.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:27.690
If he hurts himself it'll 
all be for naught.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:31.330
Well, I do get what you're saying,

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:34.540
but if this is what Bushy-Brows 
wants why not leave him be?

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.500
See ya!

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.370
That evening...

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:40.790
Thanks for the meal!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:44.270
Exhausted from another 
day of training, Lee?

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.260
Now's the time to fill up 
on your favorite food,

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.270
and take a nice long rest.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.840
I can't eat any more...

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.390
You didn't eat anything.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.520
Although I've never heard anyone
say that in their sleep before.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.800
He really does need a proper break.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.290
That is cause for concern.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.070
You think so, too, Lady Tsunade?

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:10.710
No matter how fit you are,

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.790
if you over train it will 
have the opposite effect!

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:17.180
Plus as a teenager,
Lee's body is still growing.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:20.740
Still growing... 
Why is it just his eyebrows?

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:22.350
In order to grow in a healthy way,

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:24.280
the body needs plenty of rest.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:29.890
This is definitely not balanced, 
it's nothing but hair!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.290
Look how I've grown!

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.470
It's not even him anymore!

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:36.210
But even when we tell him to rest,
he ignores us and keeps going.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:40.090
We need a way to force 
him to take it easy.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.900
<b>Labor Day</b>

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:43.900
Of course!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.610
Labor Day!

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:48.270
Labor Day?

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:52.570
Labor Day was originally 
created for laborers...

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:54.590
...and tradesmen to celebrate 
their contributions,

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:57.820
and mutually thank one 
another for their efforts.

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:00.710
Watching this doesn't make 
me feel grateful at all.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:02.740
In fact I don't even want to watch this!

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:03.840
It's too much!

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:09.120
This year, I'll order everyone 
in the village to rest.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.350
If it's a rule, Lee will have 
no choice but to comply!

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.650
Lady Tsunade...

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:16.080
Thank you very much!

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.140
And so, Labor Day came.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:24.770
The Hokage's declared that everyone
in the village has to take the day off.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.860
So make sure you actually 
rest today, Lee!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.710
Understood. I'll take the day off.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.080
Okay, that's good.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.920
He's finally learning 
the importance of rest.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:37.510
Well, since I've got the day off,

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:39.620
I'm free to train to my heart's content!

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:42.850
He hasn't learned anything!

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.090
Lee, these are Lady Tsunade's orders!

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:50.800
Think of resting as today's mission!

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:52.430
I see...

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:53.760
All right then.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.720
We demand the right to train!

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:01.190
The Hokage is taking away our 
human rights, she must go!

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:01.180
Hokage must go!

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.190
Training

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:01.190
We demand freedom

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:01.190
Retire

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.690
Enough!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.710
You just don't get it.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:10.510
Looks like he needs a lecture 
directly from Lady Tsunade.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.030
<b>Big Time Dice House</b>

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:16.090
Why did you follow me here?

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:17.990
I told you all to take the day off!

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.750
<i>She's totally in vacation mode.</i>

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.860
I don't understand the 
problem, Lady Tsunade!

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:26.590
Well for starters, the hand 
doesn't feel right...

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.570
<i>She's completely focused on the game.</i>

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.640
Hand? So I just need to rest my hands?

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.110
You mean fold?

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:35.330
You don't know anything, do you?

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.390
<i>Wait, maybe she's going to explain 
things to him after all.</i>

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.520
This is no time to lie down and quit!

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.270
The real fight starts now!

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:44.960
<i>Lady Tsunade is more 
oblivious than Lee!</i>

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:48.650
I'm really confused now. 
What will happen if I don't rest?

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:50.900
"Get too full of yourself and 
treat your underlings to lunch!

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.110
You lose your bonus!"

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:56.730
You shouldn't even have to ask...

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:58.710
You grow weak.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:01.540
<i>Lady Tsunade's mind is growing weak...</i>

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.440
<i>She won't be able to convince 
Lee in her state...</i>

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:05.900
Weak?

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.180
I'm growing weak?  No!

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:09.600
<i>I didn't expect that!</i>

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:10.750
<i>Maybe now Lee will...</i>

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:15.470
When you're this beat 
up, you have to rest...

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:20.780
<i>It's working!</i>

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.810
I can't afford to let 
my body grow weak.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.480
I have to train harder than ever!

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:28.060
Time to work!

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:31.530
That's the opposite effect!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:34.690
And now he's run off...

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:36.950
Would you please help us stop him?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.940
I told you, I say let him do as he pleases!

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:41.920
Please, we'll buy you 
all the ramen you want!

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:43.630
Sure thing, count me in!

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:45.040
Where'd you come from?!

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.820
No fair, Choji! I'm in, too!

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:49.440
That ramen is mine!

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.080
Not a chance.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.650
Those fifty bowls of ramen...

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:54.700
...and ten barbecue meals have
my name all over them!

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:56.510
I never said that!

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:04.210
I'll transform into Sakura and invite 
Bushy-Brows out to lunch.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:05.140
Then...

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:09.150
I'm so elated that you want to 
have lunch with me, Sakura!

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.150
I'll stop training right away!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.110
What could go wrong?

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:16.080
Sounds good, simple but 
practically guaranteed to work!

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:17.400
Great idea, Naruto!

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:19.690
Give Lee, Give Lee, 
leap into the fray...

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:21.880
Forget common sense, throw it all away!

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.120
Sakura?

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.480
Hey, Bushy-Brows, 
what say we grab some ramen?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.090
Naruto?

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.750
How'd you know?

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.960
Naruto, you dimwit...

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:37.930
Now it's my turn.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.610
I'll lure him in with BBQ.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:45.860
Hey, wanna grab some lunch with me?

00:18:45.860 --> 00:18:47.740
We can eat 'til we're stuffed!

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:50.690
Wow, thanks! I was just 
starting to get hungry!

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:02.010
Whew, I'm full!

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:03.850
Thanks for inviting me, Choji!

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:06.000
Now I'm all fueled up for 
my afternoon training!

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:08.230
Good luck!

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:10.240
You just wanted to eat a big lunch.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:12.250
Now he's even more motivated.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.500
Oh, sorry...

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.010
I give up!

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:19.550
You'd think all of Bushy-Brows' skits
would have you exhausted enough.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.100
Why are you still at it on your day off?

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:22.400
Skits?

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:24.100
Of course!

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:25.700
What is it, Tenten?

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.360
Those stupid skits Lee's 
always making us do!

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:31.680
We can use a skit to teach him 
the importance of proper rest!

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.070
A skit...

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.980
I'm not thrilled, but it 
may be our only shot.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:38.150
Naruto, Choji, will you help us?

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.140
If you insist.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:41.320
If at first you don't 
succeed, fry fry again.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:42.450
Try, not fry.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.990
Say it's not so, Doctor!

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.450
Is my dad really...

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:50.180
Yes...

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.170
I'm afraid he's only 
got a week, at best.

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:56.110
No...

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.590
Daddy, make sure you rest up, okay?

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:03.420
Sis, when is Lee coming home?

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:07.130
Well, I've got an old friend 
out looking for him...

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:10.090
Tenko, are you going to call him?

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:11.740
I was planning to, yes...

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:19.590
He abandoned our family to run off
and chase his foolish dreams...

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:21.730
Don't you dare call him!

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:23.990
I won't speak to him even 
if he does show up.

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:28.610
<i>We lost Mom when she was very young.</i>

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:32.820
<i>Daddy raised all three 
of us by himself.</i>

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:35.770
<i>Thanks to him, my big brother Lee was...</i>

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.300
<i>...able to pursue his dream 
of becoming an actor,</i>

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:41.760
<i>but Daddy never forgave 
him for leaving.</i>

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:47.760
<i>Still, he may talk tough, but I'm 
sure he wants to see Lee again.</i>

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:54.550
Lee, please come back...

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.680
It's been ten years...

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:03.110
Sis...

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:04.850
Great job, Tenten!

00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:06.820
There's no way Bushy-Brows 
won't be moved!

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.770
I'll stop training!

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.250
He'll be bawling!

00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:16.000
And he'll finally rest his body.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.320
We'll actually get through to Lee!

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.130
What're you all doing?

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.670
For once we get the day off, 
and you're doing skits?

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:26.890
Huh?

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:30.260
Gotta work out, see ya.

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:34.900
Don't stop the Lee!

00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:36.850
Today, Tenten and the gang learned...

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:40.520
...that no skit can move Lee 
enough to make him stop.

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:43.060
But make sure you all get 
plenty of rest, kids!

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:44.990
Lee, you butthead!

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:24.630
Next week is "Caring for 
Animals is Hard Work,"

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:26.210
<b>Caring for Animals is Hard Work
Howl at the Naruto</b>

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:26.210
and "Howl at the Naruto."

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:28.970
Okay then, I'll put my heart 
into it and howl out!

00:23:30.460 --> 00:23:32.500
Lee, it's not supposed to be literal—

00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:36.810
The Nine-Tails is reacting inside me!

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:41.790
Stop howling at each other!

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:44.150
And the Nine-Tails isn't a dog!
